  "problem": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{14}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}∼N(\\theta ,{1}^{2}),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown mean. For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{14},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}=26.8,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}^{2}=264.8.\n$$\n\nGiven that the log-likelihood function of the sample is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )+a+b\\theta +c{\\theta }^{2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n*Hint: The probability density function for a normal random variable with mean $\\theta $ and standard deviation $1$ is given by* \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{e}^{-(x-\\theta )^{2}/2},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
